From ud718c6bb1db28db2 at groups.google.com  Tue Oct 23 14:57:56 2007
From: ud718c6bb1db28db2 at groups.google.com (Steve Buckland)
Date: Tue, 23 Oct 2007 14:57:56 +0000
Subject: Re: Pooled vs. stratified for repeated transects
Message-ID: <HUoIGFexgEQ.Com7qrKE-DQJ@distance-sampling.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <HUoIGFexgEQ.29ghXqU-RwwJ@distance-sampling.groups.google.com>
References: <HUoIGFexgEQ.29ghXqU-RwwJ@distance-sampling.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/distance-sampling/c/HUoIGFexgEQ/m/Com7qrKE-DQJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Elina, the procedure in IDS is the appropriate one.  Post-stratifying by
occasion is OK if you need separate estimates of abundance for each
occasion, but these separate estimates are not independent, so if you
combine them to get an overall estimate of mean density assuming they
are independent, you will underestimate variance - as you found.  (If
you had a different set of randomised transects for each visit, then
stratification by visit would be OK.)

Steve Buckland

